body:
System Information
$ git describe --tags
4.13.0-487-g06574736b3

Detailed description
When cv::imdecodemulti() decodes a TIFF whose pages are 16-bit unsigned, 4-channel (BGRA) images with IMREAD_UNCHANGED (so wanted_channels == 4), TiffDecoder::readData() (modules/imgcodecs/src/grfmt_tiff.cpp:1085) calls the per-tile-row conversion function with explicit step = 0:
// modules/imgcodecs/src/grfmt_tiff.cpp:1085
icvCvt_BGRA2RGBA_16u_C4R(buffer16, 0,           // bgra_step = 0
    img.ptr<ushort>(img_y + i, x), 0,            // rgba_step = 0
    Size(tile_width, 1));
The step = 0 is intentional: the caller is in a per-tile-row loop (for (int i = 0; i < tile_height; i++)) and advances the row pointers itself, so it passes a single-row Size(tile_width, 1) and step = 0.
However, icvCvt_BGRA2RGBA_16u_C4R (modules/imgcodecs/src/utils.cpp:241) unconditionally applies row-step arithmetic at the end of each row iteration:
// modules/imgcodecs/src/utils.cpp:241-258
void icvCvt_BGRA2RGBA_16u_C4R( const ushort* bgra, int bgra_step,
                                ushort* rgba, int rgba_step, Size size)
{
    int i;
    for( ; size.height--; )
    {
        for( i = 0; i < size.width; i++, bgra += 4, rgba += 4 )
        {
            ushort t0 = bgra[0], t1 = bgra[1];
            ushort t2 = bgra[2], t3 = bgra[3];
            rgba[0] = t2; rgba[1] = t1;
            rgba[2] = t0; rgba[3] = t3;
        }
        bgra += bgra_step/sizeof(bgra[0]) - size.width*4;   // <-- line 255: 0/2 - width*4 = -width*4
        rgba += rgba_step/sizeof(rgba[0]) - size.width*4;   // <-- line 256: same
    }
}
With bgra_step = 0 and size.height = 1, after processing the single row the inner loop has already advanced bgra by width*4 ushorts. Line 255 then computes 0/2 - width*4 = -width*4 and adds it to bgra, subtracting
width*4 ushorts from the pointer. This is a negative unsigned offset applied to a pointer — undefined behavior per the C/C++ standard — which UBSan reports as "addition of unsigned offset overflowed".
The same pattern exists in the 8-bit variant icvCvt_BGRA2RGBA_8u_C4R (utils.cpp:236) and the other icvCvt_* helpers called with step = 0 from the same grfmt_tiff.cpp tile-decode loop. All are latent UBSan bugs; the 16u/C4 variant is the one triggered here.

API entry point: cv::imdecodemulti(InputArray buf, int flags, OutputArrayOfArrays mats) — public OpenCV imgcodecs API.
buf: encoded TIFF bytes produced by cv::imencodemulti(). All bytes are valid TIFF produced by OpenCV's own encoder — no malformed input.
flags = cv::IMREAD_UNCHANGED: documented flag that preserves the original depth and channel count, causing wanted_channels == 4 for a BGRA source.
Source image: a 1×1 CV_16UC4 (16-bit unsigned, 4-channel) cv::Mat — a valid, minimal image shape.
All API calls use legal arguments; the bug is an internal pointer-arithmetic error in the library, not API misuse.

Stack Trace
runtime error: addition of unsigned offset to 0x74e3b2be0678 overflowed to 0x74e3b2be0670
    #0 0x56d04b89656f in cv::icvCvt_BGRA2RGBA_16u_C4R(unsigned short const*, int, unsigned short*, int, cv::Size_<int>) /modules/imgcodecs/src/utils.cpp:255:11
    #1 0x56d04b85f3b7 in cv::TiffDecoder::readData(cv::Mat&) /modules/imgcodecs/src/grfmt_tiff.cpp:1085:45
    #2 0x56d04b7a1ec3 in cv::imdecodemulti_(cv::Mat const&, int, std::vector<cv::Mat, std::allocator<cv::Mat>>&, int, int) /modules/imgcodecs/src/loadsave.cpp:1576:26
    #3 0x56d04b7a1323 in cv::imdecodemulti(cv::_InputArray const&, int, std::vector<cv::Mat, std::allocator<cv::Mat>>&, cv::Range const&) /modules/imgcodecs/src/loadsave.cpp
    #4 0x56d04b3c110f in main /poc.cpp:9:7
    #5 0x78c3b38291c9 in __libc_start_call_main csu/../sysdeps/nptl/libc_start_call_main.h:58:16
    #6 0x78c3b382928a in __libc_start_main csu/../csu/libc-start.c:360:3
    #7 0x56d04b2d5bb4 in _start (/poc+0xa86bb4) (BuildId: 2ddd9da8c43971746c77ae4eb1e5936378ece83b)

SUMMARY: UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer: undefined-behavior /modules/imgcodecs/src/utils.cpp:255:11 

Steps to reproduce
PoC Code
// PoC: 16u 4-channel (BGRA) TIFF encode→decode triggers a pointer overflow in
// icvCvt_BGRA2RGBA_16u_C4R (utils.cpp:255).  TiffDecoder::readData calls it
// with step=0 (grfmt_tiff.cpp:1085); the function then computes
// bgra += 0/sizeof(ushort) - width*4, i.e. a negative offset that UBSan flags.
// All calls below are legal OpenCV API usage — no invalid arguments.
#include <opencv2/imgcodecs.hpp>
int main() {
    cv::Mat img(1, 1, CV_MAKETYPE(CV_16U, 4), cv::Scalar(0,0,0,0));
    std::vector<cv::Mat> pages = {img};
    std::vector<uint8_t> enc;
    cv::imencodemulti(".tiff", pages, enc);
    cv::Mat b(1, (int)enc.size(), CV_8U, enc.data());
    std::vector<cv::Mat> d;
    cv::imdecodemulti(b, cv::IMREAD_UNCHANGED, d);//crash
}
Steps to Reproduce
# 1. Checkout OpenCV at the pinned commit
git clone https://github.com/opencv/opencv.git
cd opencv
git checkout 06574736b35bc3f6682c3e8d52624fcac64532b9

# 2. Build OpenCV with sanitizers (Linux x86_64)
export CC=clang CXX=clang++
export CFLAGS="-fsanitize=address,undefined -fno-sanitize=function -fsanitize-address-use-after-scope -g -O0 -fstandalone-debug -fPIC -fno-omit-frame-pointer -DFUZZING_BUILD_MODE_UNSAFE_FOR_PRODUCTION"
export CXXFLAGS="$CFLAGS"
export WORK=$(pwd)/build/sanitizer

mkdir -p /tmp/opencv_build && cd /tmp/opencv_build
cmake -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX="$WORK" -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
    -DCMAKE_C_FLAGS="$CFLAGS" -DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS="$CXXFLAGS" \
    -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF -DOPENCV_FORCE_3RDPARTY_BUILD=ON \
    -DOPENCV_ENABLE_MEMORY_SANITIZER=ON \
    -DBUILD_TESTS=OFF -DBUILD_PERF_TESTS=OFF -DBUILD_EXAMPLES=OFF -DBUILD_DOCS=OFF \
    -DBUILD_opencv_apps=OFF -DWITH_IPP=OFF -DWITH_OPENCL=OFF -DWITH_TBB=OFF \
    -DWITH_EIGEN=OFF -DWITH_CUDA=OFF \
    "$SRC"   # full flag set in the bundled build/build.sh

make -j$(nproc)
make install
cp /tmp/opencv_build/3rdparty/lib/*.a "$WORK/lib/" 2>/dev/null || true

# 3. Compile the PoC (standalone, no fuzzer runtime needed)
clang++ -g -O0 -fno-omit-frame-pointer -fsanitize=address,undefined \
    -I$WORK/include/opencv4 \
    poc.cpp -o poc \
    -Wl,--start-group $WORK/lib/lib*.a -Wl,--end-group \
    -lpthread -ldl -lz

# 4. Run
./poc
Suggested Fix
The root cause is the mismatch between the caller (which passes step = 0 and advances pointers externally) and the conversion function (which unconditionally applies the step arithmetic). Two options:
Option A — skip the row-step arithmetic when step == 0 in
icvCvt_BGRA2RGBA_16u_C4R (modules/imgcodecs/src/utils.cpp):
--- a/modules/imgcodecs/src/utils.cpp
+++ b/modules/imgcodecs/src/utils.cpp
@@ -252,8 +252,10 @@ void icvCvt_BGRA2RGBA_16u_C4R( const ushort* bgra, int bgra_step,
         rgba[0] = t2; rgba[1] = t1;
         rgba[2] = t0; rgba[3] = t3;
     }
-    bgra += bgra_step/sizeof(bgra[0]) - size.width*4;
-    rgba += rgba_step/sizeof(rgba[0]) - size.width*4;
+    if (bgra_step != 0)
+        bgra += bgra_step/sizeof(bgra[0]) - size.width*4;
+    if (rgba_step != 0)
+        rgba += rgba_step/sizeof(rgba[0]) - size.width*4;
 }
The same guard should be applied to the 8-bit variant icvCvt_BGRA2RGBA_8u_C4R (utils.cpp:236) and any other icvCvt_* helper called with step = 0 from grfmt_tiff.cpp.
Option B — pass the actual row step (the real src_buffer_bytes_per_row) instead of 0 from grfmt_tiff.cpp:1085. This is more invasive and requires verifying that all callers in the tile-decode loop pass consistent steps.
Submission Statement
This report was produced by FuzzAnything's AI-assisted library fuzzer and manually verified by a team member. We reviewed the PoC against the upstream API documentation — call order, parameters, and memory ownership — and found no API misuse.

Signed-off-by: FuzzAnything fuzzanything@gmail.com

Issue submission checklist

