Detailed description
Summary
cv::minMaxIdx (and by extension cv::minMaxLoc) uses a C-style cast dispatch table where depth-specific functions with incompatible parameter types (float*, double*) are stored as a single function pointer type (void(*)(const uchar*, const uchar*, int*, int*, ...)). Calling through this mismatched pointer is undefined behaviour per the C++ standard. UBSan's indirect-call type check fires for any CV_32F or CV_64F matrix — i.e., any standard floating-point image.
