4.13.0-223-g83ea3c4242   (OpenCV 4.14.0-pre, branch 4.x)

Description
minmax.cpp:822 defines a single dispatch table function pointer type:
// minmax.cpp:822
typedef void (*MinMaxIdxFunc)(const uchar*, const uchar*, int*, int*, size_t*, size_t*, int, size_t);
The actual minMaxIdx_32f function has a completely different signature (first and third/fourth params are float*, not uchar*/int*):
// minmax.cpp:596
static void minMaxIdx_32f(const float*, const uchar*, float*, float*, size_t*, size_t*, int, size_t);
All depth-specific functions are force-cast into the table with a C-style cast that silences the compiler:
// minmax.cpp:826-832
static MinMaxIdxFunc minmaxTab[CV_DEPTH_MAX] = {
    (MinMaxIdxFunc)GET_OPTIMIZED(minMaxIdx_8u),  ...
    (MinMaxIdxFunc)GET_OPTIMIZED(minMaxIdx_32f),  // ← stored with wrong type
    (MinMaxIdxFunc)GET_OPTIMIZED(minMaxIdx_64f),  // ← stored with wrong type
    0
};
At the call site (minmax.cpp:1181), the function is invoked through the mistyped pointer:
