System Information:
OpenCV version: master (latest as of 2026-03-06, via OSS-Fuzz build)
Operating System / Platform: Ubuntu 22.04 (Linux x86_64)
Compiler & compiler version: Clang (OSS-Fuzz, with AddressSanitizer)
Detailed description
Detailed description:
A heap-buffer-overflow (READ of size 1) exists in cv::YAMLParser::parseKey() at persistence_yml.cpp:435. When parsing a YAML mapping with an empty key (e.g. : 10 at column 0),
the backward scan do c = *--endptr; while(c == ' ') always executes at least once (do-while). When endptr == ptr, the first decrement reads ptr[-1], which is 1 byte before the
heap allocation. The "empty key" check comes after the OOB read has already occurred.

Type: Heap buffer over-read (1 byte before allocation)
Severity: Low — the read value is only compared against ' ' and discarded; not exploitable.
Consequence: Undefined behavior. Triggered when any application opens a malformed YAML file via cv::FileStorage::open().

Vulnerable code path in parseKey():
char *endptr = ptr - 1, *saveptr;

do c = *++endptr;              // forward scan finds ':' immediately at ptr
while( cv_isprint(c) && c != ':' );

// endptr == ptr here (colon found at position 0)

saveptr = endptr + 1;
do c = *--endptr;              // LINE 435: backward scan decrements below ptr
while( c == ' ' );             // reads 1 byte BEFORE the buffer start

++endptr;
if( endptr == ptr )            // "empty key" check comes TOO LATE
    CV_PARSE_ERROR_CPP( "An empty key" );

ASan output:

==1==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow on address 0x7c1fcb3e068f
READ of size 1 at 0x7c1fcb3e068f thread T0
    #0 cv::YAMLParser::parseKey(char*, cv::FileNode&, cv::FileNode&)
       persistence_yml.cpp:435:16
    #1 cv::YAMLParser::parseValue(char*, cv::FileNode&, int, bool)
       persistence_yml.cpp:752:27
    #2 cv::YAMLParser::parse(char*)
       persistence_yml.cpp:842:23
    #3 cv::FileStorage::Impl::open(char const*, int, char const*)
       persistence.cpp:788:34

0x7c1fcb3e068f is located 1 bytes BEFORE 40-byte region
SUMMARY: AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow
  persistence_yml.cpp:435:16 in cv::YAMLParser::parseKey()

Suggested fix — move the empty-key check before the backward scan:

     saveptr = endptr + 1;
+    if( endptr == ptr )
+        CV_PARSE_ERROR_CPP( "An empty key" );
     do c = *--endptr;
     while( c == ' ' );

This bug was found by fixing the upstream OSS-Fuzz fuzzer filestorage_read_file_fuzzer.cc, which had its core API call storage.open() commented out (making it a complete no-op).
Fuzzer fix PR: https://github.com/google/oss-fuzz/pull/15092. After the fix, the fuzzer found this crash within 7 seconds.

### Steps to reproduce

**Steps to reproduce:**

```cpp
#include <fstream>
#include <opencv2/core.hpp>

int main() {
    // Write malformed YAML with empty key
    const char* yaml =
        "%YAML:1.0\n"
        "---\n"
        "rect:\n"
        "   x: 10\n"
        "   y: 20\n"
        "   width: 1000\n"
        ": 10\n";

    std::ofstream("/tmp/poc.yaml") << yaml;
    try {
        cv::FileStorage fs("/tmp/poc.yaml", cv::FileStorage::READ);
    } catch (const cv::Exception&) {}
    return 0;
}

g++ -fsanitize=address -g -O1 -o poc poc.cpp $(pkg-config --cflags --libs opencv4)
./poc

