System Information
OpenCV version: 4.13.0-dev
Operating System / Platform: Ubuntu 24.04
Compiler & compiler version: GCC 13.3.0
Detailed description
minEnclosingCircle cites Welzl (1991) but does not implement the random permutation that is essential to the algorithm's expected O(n) time guarantee. Without shuffling, adversarial input orderings trigger O(n³) behavior.
This is especially relevant because findContours() produces exactly such adversarial orderings — contour points are returned in sequential order along the boundary. The common pipeline findContours → minEnclosingCircle directly triggers worst-case performance.
Welzl's 1991 paper proves that if input points are randomly permuted, each point triggers a re-computation with probability at most 3/i, yielding expected O(n) time. The current code processes points in input order without shuffling, so sorted inputs hit O(n³).
Benchmark with findContours output (~5088 contour points, Release build, AVX2):



Input
Time/call




findContours output
3.93 ms


Random points (same n)
0.051 ms



Adding a Fisher-Yates shuffle (~10 lines) fixes this:



Input
Before
After




findContours output
3.93 ms
0.033 ms


Random points
0.051 ms
0.049 ms



I have a working fix with all existing tests passing and can submit a PR.
Steps to reproduce
#include <opencv2/imgproc.hpp>
#include <iostream>
#include <chrono>

int main() {
    // findContours → minEnclosingCircle
    cv::Mat img = cv::Mat::zeros(2000, 2000, CV_8UC1);
    cv::circle(img, cv::Point(1000, 1000), 900, cv::Scalar(255), -1);

    std::vector<std::vector<cv::Point>> contours;
    cv::findContours(img, contours, cv::RETR_EXTERNAL, cv::CHAIN_APPROX_NONE);

    cv::Point2f center;
    float radius;

    auto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();
    for (int r = 0; r < 5; r++)
        cv::minEnclosingCircle(contours[0], center, radius);
    auto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();

    double ms = std::chrono::duration<double, std::milli>(t1 - t0).count() / 5;
    std::cout << "findContours -> minEnclosingCircle: " << ms << " ms/call" << std::endl;
}
